**/*
!package.json
!dist/**
!icon.png
!README.md
!node_modules/highlight.js/package.json
!node_modules/highlight.js/styles/*.css
.vscode/**

# What ships and why:
#
# dist/extension.js is the bundle — src/ and lib/ are inlined into it,
# and so is highlight.js's JS, which was 389 of the 558 files this
# extension used to carry.
#
# highlight.js still needs a real directory on disk for two reasons that
# survive bundling: printer.js locates its themes with
# `require.resolve('highlight.js/package.json')`, so that file is the
# resolution anchor, and it then READS `styles/<theme>.css` at runtime.
# Bundled code cannot inline a file it opens by computed path, so the
# stylesheets ship as stylesheets.
#
# The styles are NOT narrowed to printer.js's themeList. An allowlist
# here would have to be kept in step with that array by hand, and
# loadThemes() skips a missing stylesheet silently — so drift would cost
# a theme with no error anywhere. 160 files at 186 KB is the cheaper
# side of that trade.
